{"base_rate":0.492772667542707,"brier":0.2017186596583443,"bss":0.19295673989637308,"bss_hi":0.2907179273217302,"bss_lo":0.08275401172288067,"chart":{"base":[488.0,193.1],"fp":[263.5,153.2],"lead":"62,257.6 272,230.9 482,197 692,144.2","note":{"base":"skill 0.19 — higher than 27% of cities","fp":"low end +3pp, high end +24pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.0 °C — better than 60% of cities","rel":"promised 2% → rained 5%; promised 100% → rained 80%"},"rel":"74.1,443 288,330.5 577.6,266.6 689.5,119"},"country":"JP","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.16403416557161626,"ess":444.03838771593206,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Sapporo</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Sapporo rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>80%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(2%), there is still roughly a <b>5%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 761 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 1.9 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.19, ranked 158 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(104&ndash;179) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>2%</td><td class='num'><b>5%</b></td><td class='num'>150</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>22%</td><td class='num'><b>23%</b></td><td class='num'>79</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>51%</td><td class='num'><b>41%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>74%</td><td class='num'><b>38%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>90%</td><td class='num'><b>55%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>80%</b></td><td class='num'>315</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Sapporo</b> <span class=\"muted\">Japan</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Barely beats the average</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;49% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 49% of days.</p><p>The forecast did only slightly better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.19</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>104&ndash;179\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>761 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Sapporo &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Sapporo\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"64.7968,367.44 136.32810126582277,266.8101265822785 236.9613513513513,155.72972972972974 320.247027027027,77.02702702702703 377.164347826087,28.550724637681185 410.5952380952381,18.0 410.5952380952381,22.622222222222206 377.164347826087,81.30434782608694 320.247027027027,145.89189189189187 236.9613513513513,239.35135135135135 136.32810126582277,335.9240506329114 64.7968,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"202.63074901445466\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"202.63074901445466\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"64.7968,362.58666666666664 136.32810126582277,299.0632911392405 236.9613513513513,234.43243243243242 320.247027027027,244.27027027027026 377.164347826087,181.53623188405797 410.5952380952381,89.64444444444445\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 2%&amp;#10;It rained 5% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 150 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"64.7968\" cy=\"362.58666666666664\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 22%&amp;#10;It rained 23% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 79 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"136.32810126582277\" cy=\"299.0632911392405\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 51%&amp;#10;It rained 41% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"236.9613513513513\" cy=\"234.43243243243242\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 74%&amp;#10;It rained 38% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"320.247027027027\" cy=\"244.27027027027026\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 90%&amp;#10;It rained 55% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"377.164347826087\" cy=\"181.53623188405797\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 80% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 315 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"410.5952380952381\" cy=\"89.64444444444445\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(49%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Sapporo the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.36) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (-0.43).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>34%</td><td class='num'>-0.428</td><td class='num'>36.2%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>75%</td><td class='num'>0.149</td><td class='num'>9.6%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>220</td><td class='num'>44%</td><td class='num'>0.295</td><td class='num'>17.4%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>182</td><td class='num'>46%</td><td class='num'>0.360</td><td class='num'>11.8%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":43.06667,"lon":141.35,"n":761,"n_cities":216,"name":"Sapporo","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.11,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.019200000000000002,"n":150,"obs":0.05333333333333334,"sig":true},{"hi":0.35000000000000053,"lo":0.11,"mean":0.22126582278481008,"n":79,"obs":0.22784810126582278,"sig":false},{"hi":0.64,"lo":0.35000000000000053,"mean":0.5055405405405404,"n":74,"obs":0.40540540540540543,"sig":false},{"hi":0.84,"lo":0.64,"mean":0.7408108108108107,"n":74,"obs":0.3783783783783784,"sig":true},{"hi":0.96,"lo":0.84,"mean":0.9015942028985509,"n":69,"obs":0.5507246376811594,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.96,"mean":0.996031746031746,"n":315,"obs":0.8031746031746032,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":1.9,"provisional":false,"rank":158,"rank_hi":179.0,"rank_lo":104.0,"reliability":0.040540405050132,"resolution":0.08755013108114557,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"sapporo","station":"","timezone":"Asia/Tokyo"}